-- Riso poster: two spot inks on cream paper. Warm ink: the headline and one big flat shape. Cool ink: the image
-- zone (here shapes; with a photo, the photo's shadows). Where they cross they multiply into a third colour.
Let there be a flat canvas called riso-poster, 1080 by 1666.
Let paper be #f1e9da.
Let warm be #ff4fa3.
Let cool be #2343c2.
Make the card paper, grainy 0.3, coarse.

-- the image zone: 38% down to the bottom, bleeding off the bottom and the right
Let there be a circle called sun, 330 big, at 700 860.
Make the sun warm, multiply.
Let there be 6 rectangles called stem, 90 by 760, in a row, 150 apart, from 240 1330.
Make the stems cool, multiply, 10% see-through.
Let there be 6 circles called bloom, 75 big, in a row, 150 apart, from 240 950.
Make the blooms cool, multiply.

-- the headline zone: flush left on the margin, set tight, line step 0.95 of the size, about 58% of the width
Let a line be Newsreader bold, size 158, tracking -11, aligned left, warm.
Write "Open" called h-1 as a line, at 64 200.
Write "Studio" called h-2 as a line, at 64 350.
Write "Nights" called h-3 as a line, at 64 500.
Make the h-1, the h-2 and the h-3 multiply.

-- labels: a right-hand column and a foot, caps in a geometric sans, the cool ink
Let a label be Jost 500, size 29, tracking 2, aligned left, cool.
Write "PRINT" called l-1 as a label, at 800 92.
Write "PAPER" called l-2 as a label, at 800 132.
Write "INK" called l-3 as a label, at 800 172.
Write "EAST WING" called l-4 as a label, at 800 370.
Write "STUDIO 3" called l-5 as a label, at 800 410.
Write "FRIDAYS" called l-6 as a label, at 800 482.
Write "FROM SEVEN" called l-7 as a label, at 800 522.
